# Generated Nexus BBCode. pdv_guide_bbcode.mjs writes LF and its --check gate
# byte-compares what it would write against what is on disk; with autocrlf=true
# and no rule here, git rewrites these to CRLF on checkout and every guide then
# reports a false "stale". Pin them so the gate compares like with like.
dist/nexus-articles/*.bb text eol=lf

# Release notes are copied verbatim into the release zip by
# tools/pdv_package_release.mjs, and the handoff publishes that zip's SHA256.
# Any line-ending rewrite on checkout would change the artifact's bytes and make
# the published hash unreproducible on another machine, so store these exactly as
# they ship (README is LF, CHANGELOG is CRLF) rather than normalizing either.
dist/release-meta/README.txt -text
dist/release-meta/CHANGELOG.txt -text
